    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "Parts a-c are scaffolded difference-of-squares expansions that generalise from k=1 and k=4 to symbolic k. The hardest essential demand is part d. The student must model the paddock as a square with one side lengthened and the other shortened, then map it to n=120 and k=9 and interpret the result as an area decrease. That is more than the routine expansions in p13-q6. It is slightly less than p15-q15, which asks for compare-and-explain reasoning across several computations.",
